{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED as change 1085, merged to main.\n\nBoth passages now name the two jobs that actually exist (clean-core-wheel, optional-extras), and docs/llm-framework.md records where the AST import-linter half went — its two test files run in the default suite on every matrix cell, guarded by the collection test in tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py — so a reader who remembers the deleted job does not conclude the check was dropped.\n\nOn the AC 'no reference to a per-extra, union, or import-linter JOB remains': two greps still hit, and both are intentional descriptive text rather than job references.\n  - docs/llm-framework.md: 'The AST import-linter half is no longer a dedicated job: ...' — this IS the sentence a sibling AC requires.\n  - .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:134: 'clean-core-wheel + optional-extras (per-extra venvs + union)' — verified verbatim against the job's own name: field, which is 'optional extras isolate (per-extra venvs + union)'. It describes what the single job does.\nChecked by reading the job definitions rather than trusting the grep.\n\nVerification: make lint (actionlint over all workflows) PASS; pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py 9 passed.\n\nOut of scope and deliberately untouched, both recorded in the plan and the commit:\n  - 'The optional surface is three extras' in the same docs section is stale (rebar._optional.EXTRAS holds five; grounding and metrics are missing from both the count and the bullets). Fixing it needs new descriptive content for two extras — a content change, not a mechanical job-list correction. Left for a separate ticket and noted in session log 5eb0-52a3-45f0-43e5.\n  - docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/*.jsonl matc